    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d304">

                <pb facs="0410" n="342" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v01/pg342"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72/2373½: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic"> Colonel E. M. House to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-02-14T18:35:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 14, 1916—6:35 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [Received 7:06 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Thanks for your information concerning the latest phase of the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">L</hi>[<hi rendition="#italic">usitania</hi>]
                        settlement.<anchor n="23" xml:id="d304-f1"/> Germany should, and I think
                    will, agree to German Ambassador’s latest proposal. There are so many other
                    issues involved in the controversy concerning armed merchantmen that I sincerely
                    hope you will leave it in abeyance until I return. I cannot emphasize too
                    strongly the importance of this.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Edward House</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
